      "role": "user",
      "content": "ah, yeah, i totally missed that. i'll fix the `get_next_sensor_packet` leak. \n\none more thing though—i'm also seeing some weird, non-deterministic behavior that isn't just a memory leak. sometimes the memory seems to just \"disappear\" or get corrupted in ways that don't follow a clean linear pattern. like, it's almost like the corruption is happening in the gaps between my own logic. is there any way that a memory leak could cause erratic, unpredictable behavior that doesn't just look like a standard \"out of memory\" crash? it's almost driving me crazy because it's so hard to pin down.",
